{
  "note": "How a person gets from the state they are in to something they do. Three stages, kept apart on purpose. A motivation rule says what there is to want and lets the person decide how badly. A proposal says which actions would serve a want, and most wants have several, so that no want is a disguised name for one action. A cost says what an action would take out of this particular person, which is what makes two people with the same want do different things. As in the event rules, no rule may name a member of the cast, and a condition may only ask about circumstances: everything about the person belongs in scaled_by, where it moves a weight instead of flipping a switch.",
